course: dictionary
lesson: 2237
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A coyote is a wild animal of the dog family. It is smaller than a wolf, with grey-brown fur, big ears and a bushy tail, and it lives across North and Central America. «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family and to tell other coyotes the area is taken.» Howling is one way they talk to each other.
explain: Context tells you which meaning the writer means. In a science text about deserts and prairies, coyote means the animal. In the USA it can also be slang for a person paid to smuggle people secretly across the border from Mexico. Check the clues: if the text is about habitats, food or howling, it is the animal.
explain: Do not mix up real coyotes with cartoon characters. «Coyote never catches him, however many ACME rockets he buys.» That is Wile E. Coyote, a cartoon who always fails. «But a real coyote can run more than twice as fast» than a roadrunner. Real coyotes do not use tools; they hunt by stalking, chasing and pouncing.
fact: A coyote is a wild animal of the dog family, smaller than a wolf.
fact: Coyotes live in deserts, prairies, forests and even big cities across North and Central America.
fact: Coyotes eat almost anything, such as mice, rabbits, fruit and rubbish.
fact: «Coyote» is also US slang for a person paid to smuggle people across the border from Mexico.
fact: In Native American stories, Coyote is a clever trickster, and in cartoons Wile E. Coyote always chases the Road Runner and fails.
exercise: According to the lesson, a coyote is smaller than which animal? | A horse | A bear | *A wolf
exercise: «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family.» Why do coyotes howl? | To swim across rivers | To look for tools | To catch roadrunners with ACME rockets | *To keep in touch and tell others the area is taken
exercise: «Real coyotes do not use tools; they hunt by stalking, chasing and pouncing.» How do real coyotes hunt? | They fly down from trees | *By stalking, chasing and pouncing | They build traps with ropes | They use ACME rockets
test: In the cartoon, what happens to Wile E. Coyote? | He catches the Road Runner every time | He becomes friends with the bird | *He never catches the Road Runner, however many rockets he buys | He runs away to the mountains
test: Which clue tells you a text is about the animal, not the slang? | Smuggling people across a border | *Deserts, prairies and eating mice | Coming from Mexico
exam: Which clue shows that coyote means the animal, not the slang? | *Howling and yipping at night in the desert | Smuggling people secretly | Coming from Mexico into the USA | Paid to move people across a border
